# Environment file for the firewall-agent systemd service.
#
# Copy this file to /etc/default/firewall-agent on the target machine and
# set FIREWALL_API_URL for that machine's environment. This file is only an
# example/template - it is not installed automatically by install.sh, and
# the real /etc/default/firewall-agent is not tracked in git, since the
# correct URL is specific to each deployment (dev VM vs. real deployment).
#
# Example for a Ubuntu VM whose Node.js API runs on the Windows host under
# VirtualBox NAT networking (10.0.2.2 is the VirtualBox NAT gateway address
# that reaches the host machine from inside the guest):
#
# FIREWALL_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3000/api/firewall/rules?type=ip

# FIREWALL_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=10
